Email Phishing - 
Criminals use this method by sending fake emails prentending to be trusted sources/organisations to steal sensitive information, they often request login credentials, banking details and personal IDs.Example: An email claiming to be from a bank telling customers to click on the link to update their KYC.


Speae Phishing - 
A form of phishing attack aimed at a specific individual or an organisation. Criminals use professinla information to appear legitimate, Example: An example sent to an employee appearing to be from the manager request for access to confedentila files.


Smishing - 
A form of phishing where criminals send fake SMS or text messages which contain fradulent links or fake alerts that steal credentials and OTPs. Example:A text sent to a victim message claming they won a sum of money from a competition and they should press the link to verify their identity.
